{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/514554-new-contract-needing-input-infant-games","id":514554,"title":"New Contract. Needing input. Infant Games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-14T15:29:28-07:00","id":514554,"title":"New Contract. Needing input. Infant Games","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Welcoming input and thoughts.<br /> <br /> <b>Contracts of Infant Games</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>\u25cf Jingly-keys</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:1 Glamour</b><br /> <b>Dice Pool: Dexterity + Socialize </b><br /> <b>Action: instant</b><br /> <b>Catch: You actually use a set of keys to distract the target.</b><br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: You become distracted for 1 action, instead of the target.</b><br /> <b>Failure: The target is not distracted.</b><br /> <b>Success: One target is distracted for 1 action due to fright or laughter. They will not take actions in their next turn as they are distracted by whatever caught their eye. This clause can only be used on 1 target once per scene. </b><br /> <b>Exceptional Success: The target is distracted for a number of actions equal to the number of successes rolled. </b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <br /> <b>\u25cf\u25cf Answer the Phone</b></span><br /> <b>Cost: 2 Glamour</b><br /> <b>Dice Pool: Manipulation + Empathy</b><br /> <b>Action: instant </b><br /> <b>Catch: You use a toy phone</b><br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: The call connects to someone other than the intended target without your knowledge, Storytellers choice. </b><br /> <b>Failure: The call fails to connect for whatever reason. </b><br /> <b>Success: You make contact with intended target via a fake phone, either toy or hand. The recipient of the phone call must have a phone, toy or otherwise, nearby to answer. This phone contact will work with anyone who speaks into the phone. This phone call is limited in time to 1 minute per success.</b><br /> <b>Exceptional Success: No extra benefit beyond an extra long phone call. </b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Peek-a-Boo </b></span><br /> <b>Cost: 2 Glamour</b><br /> <b>Dice Pool: Manipulation + Expression</b><br /> <b>Action: instant</b><br /> <b>Catch: You are able to conceal at least 50% of your person from the target including your face. </b><br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: The clause reverses and you lose track of the target until the end of the scene, but they can still see you. </b><br /> <b>Failure: The target sees through the deception and there is no result. </b><br /> <b>Success: You obscure your presence from the target for the remainder of the scene. They cannot affect you and you cannot affect them. If you attack the target in any way, you receive half the damage dealt yourself; the Wyrd does not take kindly to attacking a \u201cchild\u201d and this translates over to targets of this clause; even if they are adults.</b><br /> <b>Exceptional Success: The target will not be able to see or interact with you until the sun rises or sets next. </b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Convincing Adult</b></span><br /> <b>Cost: 2 Glamour + 1 will power point</b><br /> <b>Dice Pool: Presence + Persuasion vs. Resolve + Composure</b><br /> <b>Action: instant </b><br /> <b>Catch: The targets parent or mentor is present.</b><br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: The target knows that anything they say will be accepted as truth to you for the remainder of the scene. </b><br /> <b>Failure: Nothing happens</b><br /> <b>Success: You are able to convince the target of anything you wish. They are still able to make their own decisions, but they will believe anything you say and accept it as fact, no matter how outlandish it may seem. The effects last for the remainder of the scene.</b><br /> <b>Exceptional Success: Your deceit is so perfect that the target will believe it utterly and indefinitely. </b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Got Yer Nose </b></span><br /> <b>Cost: 3 glamour</b><br /> <b>Dice Pool: Wits + Subterfuge vs. Wits + Dexterity </b><br /> <b>Action: instant</b><br /> <b>Catch: You are performing this clause strictly for entertainment value. </b><br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: Your corresponding body part falls off your person instead of the targets, and cannot be replaced for the remainder of the scene. </b><br /> <b>Failure: Nothing happens</b><br /> <b>Success: You actually remove a body part from the target. No pain is experienced, no damage is dealt, and no blood issues forth from either wound (ie it comes off completely healed over with skin when removed). The part remains removed until it is physically replaced or the scene ends. This may result in penalties appropriately assigned by the story teller. </b><br /> <b>Use of this clause will not result in the targets death, even if you remove their head. </b><br /> <b>You can remove your own body parts if you wish; your thumb for example. </b><br /> <b>Exceptional Success: The removal can be permanent if you wish, for the expenditure of 1willpower dot. </b><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5989-druidspath","name":"druidspath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T21:32:02-07:00","id":514773,"title":"","content":"Contracts tend to have Wyrd or Mantle in their dice pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T01:21:56-07:00","id":514904,"title":"","content":"Hahahahah, well those are simply great! Love it! Convincing Adult feels a bit weird next to the others, but otherwise seems quite solid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T09:47:20-07:00","id":515256,"title":"","content":"Yea, I was running out of ideas. The thought process being games you would play with a toddler. My 13 year old pointed out a game I play with my nieces and nephews where I tell them that I am going to bring them to my house to live with me from now on. Sometimes they are all for it, some times there is the response &quot;no, I stay with mommy&quot;<br /> <br /> Other games considered were &quot;Chase&quot; and &quot;raspberries/zerberts&quot; but couldnt find a way to make them work. I am wide open to suggestions.<br /> <br /> I am concerned about the cost for exceptional success on clause #5 &quot;Got your nose&quot; Paying a willpower DOT, seems like a big cost, but a willpower point is too little. Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5989-druidspath","name":"druidspath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T12:10:21-07:00","id":515334,"title":"","content":"The Floor is Lava?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T15:45:34-07:00","id":515514,"title":"","content":"yea, that was considered, but I was trying to keep it to games one would play with an infant or toddler. I could think of another contract for kids games of imagination. With clauses like Hide and Go Seek, The floor is lava, Build a fort, and so on. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5989-druidspath","name":"druidspath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T14:14:37-07:00","id":516450,"title":"","content":"How about tickle monster? Creepy mouse? Patty-Cake? This little piggy went to market?<br /> <br /> EDIT: it occurs to me some of these games are probably culturally specific. Like, my grandma had a few of these that involved specific rhymes or chants like party-cake or creepy mouse, but were in Spanish, and I assume would not be familiar to most people who didn't grow up in Puerto Rican families.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-16-2015, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T15:30:28-07:00","id":516509,"title":"","content":"Good Suggestions Charlaquin. I dont know what Creepy Mouse is, but how would the others look in Clause form? Something in the **** dot range to replace the other one<br /> ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5989-druidspath","name":"druidspath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T17:36:20-07:00","id":516575,"title":"","content":"That's a tough question. I could see patty-cake using Dexterity in the dice pool, maybe Dexterity (to properly perform the hand movements) + Expression (to recite the poem), contested by Composure (to keep up) + Empathy (to intuit the aggressor's next move and synchronize your own movements with them). And then the loser suffers some sort of consequence for breaking the pattern?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:23:31-07:00","id":518507,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Patty-Cake</b></span><br /> <b>Cost: 2 Glamour </b><br /> <b>Dice Pool: Dex + Expression vs. Composure + Empathy</b><br /> <b>Action: contested </b><br /> <b>Catch: The targets parent or mentor is present.</b><br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: You spend the rest of the scene mimicking the target</b><br /> <b>Failure: Nothing happens</b><br /> <b>Success: The target replicates your movements for the remainder of the scene. </b><br /> <b>Exceptional Success: The control over your target is so absloute that you now have controll over their speech as well as their movements. </b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5989-druidspath","name":"druidspath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:24:06-07:00","id":518508,"title":"","content":"Like this ^^^ Charlaquin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5989-druidspath","name":"druidspath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:34:01-07:00","id":518522,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that looks pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:57:56-07:00","id":518535,"title":"","content":"Refined contract looks like this: <br /> <br /> <br /> Contracts of Infant Games<br /> \u25cf Jingly-keys<br /> <b>Cost:</b>1 Glamour<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Dexterity + Socialize<br /> <b>Action:</b> instant<br /> <b>Catch:</b> You actually use a set of keys to distract the target.<br /> <b>Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure:</b> You become distracted for 1 action, instead of the target.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: The target is not distracted.<br /> <b>Success:</b> One target is distracted for 1 action due to fright or laughter. They will not take actions in their next turn as they are distracted by whatever caught their eye. This clause can only be used on 1 target once per scene.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The target is distracted for a number of actions equal to the number of successes rolled.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf Answer the Phone<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Glamour<br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation + Empathy<br /> <b>Action</b>: instant<br /> <b>Catch:</b> You use a toy phone<br /> <b>Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure:</b> The call connects to someone other than the intended target without your knowledge, Storytellers choice.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The call fails to connect for whatever reason.<br /> <b>Success:</b> You make contact with intended target via a fake phone, either toy or hand. The recipient of the phone call must have a phone, toy or otherwise, nearby to answer. This phone contact will work with anyone who speaks into the phone. This phone call is limited in time to 1 minute per success.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> No extra benefit beyond an extra long phone call.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Peek-a-Boo<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Glamour<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Expression<br /> <b>Action:</b> instant<br /> <b>Catch:</b> You are able to conceal at least 50% of your person from the target including your face.<br /> <b>Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure:</b> The clause reverses and you lose track of the target until the end of the scene, but they can still see you.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The target sees through the deception and there is no result.<br /> <b>Success:</b> You obscure your presence from the target for the remainder of the scene. They cannot affect you and you cannot affect them. If you attack the target in any way, you receive half the damage dealt yourself; the Wyrd does not take kindly to attacking a \u201cchild\u201d and this translates over to targets of this clause; even if they are adults.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The target will not be able to see or interact with you until the sun rises or sets next.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Patty-Cake<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Glamour<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Dex + Expression vs. Composure + Empathy<br /> <b>Action:</b> contested<br /> <b>Catch:</b> The targets parent or mentor is present.<br /> <b>Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure:</b> You spend the rest of the scene mimicking the target<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Nothing happens<br /> <b>Success:</b> The target replicates your movements for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The control over your target is so absolute that you now have control over their speech as well as their movements.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Got Yer Nose<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3 glamour<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Subterfuge vs. Wits + Dexterity<br /> <b>Action:</b> instant<br /> <b>Catch:</b> You are performing this clause strictly for entertainment value.<br /> <b>Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure:</b> Your corresponding body part falls off your person instead of the targets, and cannot be replaced for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Nothing happens<br /> <b>Success:</b> You actually remove a body part from the target. No pain is experienced, no damage is dealt, and no blood issues forth from either wound (ie it comes off completely healed over with skin when removed). The part remains removed until it is physically replaced or the scene ends. This may result in penalties appropriately assigned by the story teller.<br /> Use of this clause will not result in the targets death, even if you remove their head.<br /> You can remove your own body parts if you wish; your thumb for example.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The removal can be permanent if you wish, for the expenditure of 1willpower dot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5989-druidspath","name":"druidspath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T06:15:18-07:00","id":521745,"title":"","content":"Patty-Cake is great-- I would have called it &quot;Simon Says&quot; or &quot;Stop Hitting Yourself&quot; but that's just me. For four dots, I would have been tempted to create a &quot;Ring Around the Rosy&quot; contract that would cause a group of people to &quot;all fall down.&quot; The use of ashes or a posy would be the catch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T09:07:45-07:00","id":521940,"title":"","content":"You know, with the changes to Contract structure in 2e, you could make all of these into Contracts with a related theme, instead of being limited to five Clauses of a single Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T06:25:02-07:00","id":523120,"title":"","content":"Personaly, Im kinda pissed about 2e, im just now (after 7 years) getting a good grip on current edition. and I am about to start a new, long term game, bad timing. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5989-druidspath","name":"druidspath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T16:11:21-07:00","id":523772,"title":"","content":"1e had a very good, long run, I'm sorry you didn't get to the point where you were comfortable with the rules in that time. Fortunately, 1e still exists, and there's nothing to stop you from playing it (a lot of the regulars on these forums still do), and even better, the two editions are similar enough mechanically that you can easily use your favorite parts of both (also something a lot of our regulars do).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T17:20:54-07:00","id":523809,"title":"","content":"Neglected to pipe up earlier, but I came into this thread confused and dubious, and left really liking what you did here. ^_^ Good work on these!<br /> <br /> And agreed with Charlaquin. I have no doubt that after 2e's released, this board will have a thread or two describing favored splices from between editions as well as some other food for thought on the topic. Likewise, there will be threads here about things in 2e that don't click for people, which may likewise help you and anyone else get accustomed to how 2e ticks.<br /> <br /> Unless you meant more in the sense of, &quot;We'll probably be starting before 2e comes out, which means 1e's rules even if something about 2e catches our eyes.&quot; Which is its own kind of unfortunate. Still, if the group's amenable to making changes to the game's mechanics mid-game, that could be a way to make adjustments if you decide that's best. Alternatively, it wouldn't be the first campaign that's paired changes from a new edition with some big, dramatic plot that culminates in a change to the way the world/splats work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Forumites can be helpful with other suggestions, once we know how 2e works. Fingers crossed that you'll find something that works out for you and your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T21:09:19-07:00","id":523963,"title":"","content":"That does stink about the timing, though. And since it's so difficult to accurately project a release date, it's not like you can say &quot;2e will be out in [month] so let's play a short Geist chronicle in the mean time and decide which edition to use for our Changeling game after we've all had a chance to decide what rules we want to use.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T00:49:19-07:00","id":524150,"title":"","content":"I think that Jingly-Keys is overpowered for a one dot clause. Compare it to Every Sorrow a Jewel, the five dot Fleeting Winter Clause. Every Sorrow a Jewel has a higher cost (3 Glamour + 1 Willpower), a much more difficult catch (the target has to have tasted one of your tears), and has only slightly improved effects (unlike Jingly-Keys it isn't restricted to once per scene per target and can take away multiple actions without an exceptional success). I don't think the slightly weaker effect can justify a four dot drop in the level of the Clause, especially given how much cheaper Jingly-Keys is to use (that catch is so easy, it's essentially free). If you are going to keep it, you'll at least want to mention that the target keeps their Defense or that attacking the target breaks the effect. Personally, I'd change Jingly-Keys so that the target is distracted by the Changeling using the Clause and suffers a penalty to any perception tests to notice anything else. This way the clause is still very useful (you could use it to distract a guard while your motley mate sneaks past or steals his gun for instance) and makes sense thematically, but isn't as close in power to a five dot clause.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I think it's worth pointing out that, as written, you could use Got Your Nose to permanently remove someone's head on an exceptional success!<br /> <br /> Also, I'd consider changing the name of the Contract to Playtime. Infant Games just sounds kind of weird to me.<br /> <br /> Really rough ideas for other Clauses that might be cool:<br /> I'm going to count to 3 - The target suffers a cumulative penalty (up to 3, obviously) each turn that it continues to perform the action you designate. The catch is scolding the target and counting each turn. Stops working after you get to 3. Maybe 1 dot.<br /> Take Turns (or Sharing is Caring) - The target gives you whatever item it is currently using so that you can &quot;have a turn&quot;. Probably 2 dots. You could offer a toy in exchange to activate the catch.<br /> Go to Your Room - Forces the target to leave the scene if it is able. Probably be 3 or 4 dots. Catch could trigger if the target is in their own house and can actually go to their bedroom.<br /> Time Out - If you really want a Clause that causes the target to lose actions, this could be a 4 or 5 dot clause that makes them unable to take physical actions but still allows defense. The catch could involve the target throwing a tantrum.<br /> Play Nice - Stops a combat for a scene. Probably 5 dots. The combatants must all be your students or children to activate the catch.<br /> <br /> Actually, now that I look at them, the above Clauses could make up their own Contract - a sort of companion to Infant Games/Playtime. It could be called Contracts of Scolding maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T12:00:05-07:00","id":524610,"title":"","content":"Thanks CSSchultz, fair to point out on some things.<br /> <br /> I like your ideas of Scolding<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5989-druidspath","name":"druidspath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}